## Detailed Findings

### Prometheus (Go) - Already Cached

**File:** `model/labels/matcher.go`

The current implementation:
```go
// Lines 47-53: Matcher struct already has compiled regex cache
type Matcher struct {
    Type  MatchType
    Name  string
    Value string
    re *FastRegexMatcher  // ✅ Cached compiled regex
}

// Lines 107-120: Matches method - uses cached regex
func (m *Matcher) Matches(s string) bool {
    switch m.Type {
    case MatchRegexp:
        return m.re.MatchString(s)  // Uses cached regex
    ...
    }
}
```

The change needed: Change signature from `Matches(s string) bool` to `Matches(s string) (bool, error)` to surface any regex compilation errors.

### Grafana Alerting (TypeScript) - Needs Fixing

**File:** `packages/grafana-alerting/src/grafana/matchers/utils.ts`

The problematic code (lines 107-116):
```typescript
// ❌ PROBLEM: Re-compiles regex on EVERY call
'=~': (lv, mv) => {
    const valueWithFlagsParsed = parseFlags(`^(?:${mv})$`);
    const re = new RegExp(valueWithFlagsParsed.cleaned, valueWithFlagsParsed.flags);  // NEW regex each time!
    return re.test(lv);
},
'!~': (lv, mv) => {
    const valueWithFlagsParsed = parseFlags(`^(?:${mv})$`);
    const re = new RegExp(valueWithFlagsParsed.cleaned, valueWithFlagsParsed.flags);  // NEW regex each time!
    return !re.test(lv);
},
```

Error handling (lines 89-97):
```typescript
try {
    return matchFunction(labelValue, value);
} catch (err) {
    return false;  // ❌ Silently swallows errors instead of surfacing them
}
```

